{"type":"text","timestamp":1790886752456,"sessionID":"ses_f06d58c82ffep16tG2ouS2XTmY","part":{"id":"prt_0f92af119001w0x5kTi7FE3lBP","messageID":"msg_0f92ac6be001798dtSuQELylYw","sessionID":"ses_f06d58c82ffep16tG2ouS2XTmY","type":"text","text":"I now have all the relevant source. The control flow in `BaseRetrying._begin_iter`, `_post_retry_check_actions`, and `_post_stop_check_actions`, plus `Retrying.__call__`, answers all four questions directly.\n\n{\"action\":\"finish\",\"answer\":{\"after_runs_on_accepted_success\":{\"value\":false,\"citations\":[{\"path\":\"tenacity/__init__.py\",\"quote\":\"def _post_retry_check_actions(self, retry_state: \\\"RetryCallState\\\") -> None:\\n        if not (self.iter_state.is_explicit_retry or self.iter_state.retry_run_result):\\n            self._add_action_func(lambda rs: rs.outcome.result())\\n            return\\n\\n        if self.after is not None:\\n            self._add_action_func(self.after)\"},{\"path\":\"tenacity/__init__.py\",\"quote\":\"if not self.iter_state.is_explicit_retry:\\n            self._add_action_func(self._run_retry)\\n        self._add_action_func(self._post_retry_check_actions)\"}]},\"wait_computed_before_stop\":{\"value\":true,\"citations\":[{\"path\":\"tenacity/__init__.py\",\"quote\":\"self._add_action_func(self._run_wait)\\n        self._add_action_func(self._run_stop)\\n        self._add_action_func(self._post_stop_check_actions)\"},{\"path\":\"tenacity/__init__.py\",\"quote\":\"def _run_wait(self, retry_state: \\\"RetryCallState\\\") -> None:\\n        ...\\n        if not self.wait:  # type: ignore[truthy-bool]\\n            retry_state.upcoming_sleep = 0.0\\n        else:\\n            retry_state.upcoming_sleep = self.wait(retry_state)\\n\\n    def _run_stop(self, retry_state: \\\"RetryCallState\\\") -> None:\\n        self.statistics[\\\"delay_since_first_attempt\\\"] = retry_state.seconds_since_start\\n        self.iter_state.stop_run_result = self.stop(retry_state)\"},{\"path\":\"tenacity/__init__.py\",\"quote\":\"for action in self.iter_state.actions:\\n            result = action(retry_state)\"}]},\"before_sleep_runs_when_stopped\":{\"value\":false,\"citations\":[{\"path\":\"tenacity/__init__.py\",\"quote\":\"def _post_stop_check_actions(self, retry_state: \\\"RetryCallState\\\") -> None:\\n        if self.iter_state.stop_run_result:\\n            if self.retry_error_callback:\\n                self._add_action_func(self.retry_error_callback)\\n                return\\n\\n            def exc_check(rs: \\\"RetryCallState\\\") -> None:\\n                fut = t.cast(\\\"Future\\\", rs.outcome)\\n                retry_exc = self.retry_error_cls(fut)\\n                if self.reraise:\\n                    retry_exc.reraise()\\n                raise retry_exc from fut.exception()\\n\\n            self._add_action_func(exc_check)\\n            return\"},{\"path\":\"tenacity/__init__.py\",\"quote\":\"if self.before_sleep is not None:\\n            self._add_action_func(self.before_sleep)\\n\\n        self._add_action_func(lambda rs: DoSleep(rs.upcoming_sleep))\"}]},\"retry_error_callback_replaces_exhaustion_error\":{\"value\":true,\"citations\":[{\"path\":\"tenacity/__init__.py\",\"quote\":\"if self.iter_state.stop_run_result:\\n            if self.retry_error_callback:\\n                self._add_action_func(self.retry_error_callback)\\n                return\"},{\"path\":\"tenacity/__init__.py\",\"quote\":\"def iter(self, retry_state: \\\"RetryCallState\\\") -> DoAttempt | DoSleep | t.Any:\\n        self._begin_iter(retry_state)\\n        result = None\\n        for action in self.iter_state.actions:\\n            result = action(retry_state)\\n        return result\"},{\"path\":\"tenacity/__init__.py\",\"quote\":\"do = self.iter(retry_state=retry_state)\\n            if isinstance(do, DoAttempt):\\n                try:\\n                    result = fn(*args, **kwargs)\\n                except BaseException:\\n                    retry_state.set_exception(sys.exc_info())  # type: ignore[arg-type]\\n                else:\\n                    retry_state.set_result(result)\\n            elif isinstance(do, DoSleep):\\n                retry_state.prepare_for_next_attempt()\\n                self.sleep(do)\\n            else:\\n                return do  # type: ignore[no-any-return]\"}]},\"notes\":\"Synchronous flow (Retrying.__call__ -> iter -> _begin_iter/_post_retry_check_actions/_post_stop_check_actions): after a completed attempt, _run_retry evaluates the retry predicate; if it is false (accepted result or exception not selected for retry), the result is returned/raised immediately via 'lambda rs: rs.outcome.result()' with an early return, so 'after' never runs on an accepted success (1: False). When a retry is to be considered, actions are queued in the order _run_wait then _run_stop, and iter() executes them in queue order, so upcoming_sleep (the wait duration) is computed before stop() is evaluated (2: True; this is what lets stop_before_delay consult the computed delay). In _post_stop_check_actions, if stop_run_result is true, only retry_error_callback or the exc_check raising action is queued and the function returns before before_sleep/DoSleep are ever queued, so before_sleep does not run on the final stopped attempt (3: False). When retry_error_callback is configured, it becomes the last action and its return value becomes the result of iter(), which Retrying.__call__ returns via 'return do', so the callback's return value replaces the usual RetryError (4: True; without it, exc_check raises retry_error_cls or reraises). This is a source reading of tenacity/__init__.py, not a formal proof.\"}}","time":{"start":1790886736153,"end":1790886752439}}}
